                        <origin>
                            <!--
                                TODO: rethink encoding of dates so this is consistent and applicable for a range or projects

                                first thoughts:

                                - almost all inscriptions fall into pre-Gregorian times
                                - nobody ever computes precise duration on ancient dates, so W3C considerations about processing of dates are not that important
                                - very few inscriptions have precise date down to a day, therefore 11days difference between Julian and Gregorian is inconsequential
                                - for notBefore/notAfter or when with just a year or year-month, difference between Julian and Gregorian is also pretty much inconsequential

                                potential solution: 

                                - use `notBefore/notAfter` together with `@calendar` (if at all necessary); skip `@when` and use the text content of the element to provide any remarks on the date
                                - for very rare cases when precise date is available use `when-custom` and `datingMethod`

                                This way all date ranges are *always* in notBefore/notAfter; 
                                we only have one set of dating attributes to process for machine-readable
                                we match typical way of encoding dates (although there are exceptions that use the *-custom even for date ranges)

                                ISicily http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/services/inscription/ISic000001.xml
                                <origDate datingMethod="#julian" notBefore-custom="0050" notAfter-custom="0300" evidence="lettering textual-context">between later 1st and 3rd century CE</origDate>

                                PYU Inscriptions https://zenodo.org/records/1207290

                                <origDate calendar="Julian" notBefore="0200" notAfter="1300" precision="medium">Undated. Certainly no earlier than 200 CE, and unlikely to be later than 1300. </origDate>
                                
                                26) und 27) Datierung (zusammenfassen?)

                                @when-custom - Korrekte Datumsangabe, entweder nur Jahr oder xs:date YYYY-MM-DD
                                @notBefore-custom - wie @when aber gemeint als "nach"
                                @notAfter-custom - wie @when aber gemeint als "vor"
                                Im Content - falls exakte Datierung unmöglich; schließt die anderen Attribute aus
                                @datingMethod - fixes Attribut, hier immer Julianisch
                            -->
                            <origDate when-custom="" notBefore-custom="" notAfter-custom="" datingMethod="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julian_calendar"/>
                            <!-- in @corresp wird die GeoID angegeben, andere Ortsangaben sind redundant und werden
                                am Ende nur hinein kopiert - siehe Kommentare -->
                            <origPlace corresp=""/>
                        </origin>
                        <!--
                            11) Fundjahr (Attribute auf <provenance>)

                            @when - Korrekte Datumsangabe, entweder nur Jahr oder xs:date YYYY-MM-DD
                            @notBefore - wie @when aber gemeint als "nach"
                            @notAfter - wie @when aber gemeint als "vor"
                            @when-custom - falls exakte Datierung unmöglich; schließt die anderen Attribute aus
